        "description": "Bloomberg Daybreak Europe is your essential morning viewing to stay ahead. Live from London, we set the agenda for your day, catching you up with overnight markets news from the US and Asia. And we'll tell you what matters for investors in Europe, giving you insight before trading begins.\n\nOn today's show, US Secretary of State Marco Rubio is to meet Hungarian Prime Minister Viktor Orban today in Budapest. This comes after Rubio said in a Bloomberg interview that Europe's fate is intertwined with the US while faulting the continent for a decline in Western values.\n\nIsraeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu has proposed terms for any deescalation deal with Iran during a meeting with US President Donald Trump. It includes Iran not possessing enriched material and a limit on Iranian ballistic missiles.\n\nWarner Bros. is said to be weighing reopening sale talks with Paramount after receiving its latest hostile offer. (Source: Bloomberg)",
